{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/399247-your-dark-eras-list","id":399247,"title":"Your Dark Eras list","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-09T13:54:17-08:00","id":399247,"title":"Your Dark Eras list","content":"List your settings you want to see in Dark Eras for werewolf<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Viking Werewolf (I still hope and pray they bring it back. I went bonkers when it was reveal)</li> <li>Edo period, Japan (Samurai werewolves!)</li> <li>Roman Empire (Hoping and praying it wins\u2026)</li> <li>Teotihuacan period or Aztec Empire (I know, I know skinchangers got that era but I hope werewolf can too, working on my own project)</li> <li>American Revolution</li> <li>The Gold Rush</li> <li>Han Dynasty</li> <li>Hellenistic Civilization</li> </ol>That\u2019s what I can think of so far. Anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 02-09-2015, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:03:26-08:00","id":399273,"title":"","content":"9)Mongolian Werewolves during the reign of Gengis Khan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:05:47-08:00","id":399303,"title":"","content":"&quot;You are[list belonging to someone named Dark Eras.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know proper use of apostrophes is hard, but it's well worth the effort.<br /> <br /> I'm not gonna stop banging on my Meiji Restoration drum; the samurai class is abolished, the Japanese Wolf goes extinct, and tradition falls by the wayside as European ideals and technology drags Japan into the modern age. As Father Wolf had to die so that his duty could be performed by the better-abled, so too must old Japan die so that the nation can stand on the global stage. The Uratha are ronin, wandering without masters and trying to keep the balance between ancient kami and spirits of Western machines.<br /> <br /> It's Werewolf through Kurasawa's lens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T15:33:04-08:00","id":399418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/399247-your-dark-eras-list?p=399273#post399273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9)Mongolian Werewolves during the reign of Gengis Khan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! That's nice!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You are[list belonging to someone named Dark Eras.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know proper use of apostrophes is hard, but it's well worth the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I just got out of class and my brain is a little tire, my bad.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T21:50:14-08:00","id":399964,"title":"","content":"Yeah in order, viking age werewolf, Roman era werewolf, Sumerian werewolf, possibly wild west (may as well just go with apocalypse though) Honestly I wouldn't mind a world of darkness version of Clive Barker's Jericho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T23:02:05-08:00","id":400026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/399247-your-dark-eras-list#post399247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">List your settings you want to see in Dark Eras for werewolf<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Teotihuacan period or Aztec Empire (I know, I know skinchangers got that era but I hope werewolf can too, working on my own project)</li> <li>Hellenistic Civilization</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>You get that with <b>Skinchangers</b> and <b>Mage</b> Eras with &quot;Other supernatural&quot; sidebar every Era will have. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:50:14-08:00","id":400816,"title":"","content":"Hey, a guy can still dream <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Though kind of envious of Mage since there getting pretty awesome settings. Please bring Viking Werewolf back!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T10:16:02-08:00","id":402005,"title":"","content":"Anything in human prehistory through the Bronze Age. Something I particularly would like to see are Werewolves during the settling of the Old World and New World by humanity \u2014 the tribes were said to have formed during this era, if I remember the canon right. The Iron Masters would have been incredibly interesting during this point, in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T10:46:16-08:00","id":402062,"title":"","content":"World War II. I want to see Werewolves in that kind of setting so bad it hurts. Ever since I read the piece of fiction on page 27 of Tribes of the Moon, I've wanted to see more. It was a short story, but it sparked my creative energies and I've been planning a WWII game since. I just haven't had the chance to run it yet, sadly. But I want more of what that story had. It would be kinda &quot; Pulp Hero&quot;, but that's fine for me, though I know that might not work for others.<br /> <br /> Or better yet, why not a crossover setting focusing on WWII? How did it effect the supernaturals? How did THEY effect it? Just thought I'd throw that out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T09:45:04-08:00","id":403406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/399247-your-dark-eras-list?p=399303#post399303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not gonna stop banging on my Meiji Restoration drum; the samurai class is abolished, the Japanese Wolf goes extinct, and tradition falls by the wayside as European ideals and technology drags Japan into the modern age. As Father Wolf had to die so that his duty could be performed by the better-abled, so too must old Japan die so that the nation can stand on the global stage. The Uratha are ronin, wandering without masters and trying to keep the balance between ancient kami and spirits of Western machines.<br /> <br /> It's Werewolf through Kurasawa's lens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, there were two species of Japanese wolf, the Hokkaido and the Honshu, with the Honshu wolf surviving until 1905. There are still bigfoot-like sightings of the Honshu wolf to this day. And the more I read about the roles of wolves (both subspecies) in Japanese folklore, the more I know that we NEED Meiji Period Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","user":"Daydreamer","date":". 02-12-2015, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T12:40:12-08:00","id":403593,"title":"","content":"Might lead to a tabletop version of Wolf Children. Not that that would be terrible at all. Book/movie was pretty great (as a werewolf fan)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T14:38:48-08:00","id":403726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/399247-your-dark-eras-list?p=402062#post402062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">World War II. I want to see Werewolves in that kind of setting so bad it hurts. Ever since I read the piece of fiction on page 27 of Tribes of the Moon, I've wanted to see more. It was a short story, but it sparked my creative energies and I've been planning a WWII game since. I just haven't had the chance to run it yet, sadly. But I want more of what that story had. It would be kinda &quot; Pulp Hero&quot;, but that's fine for me, though I know that might not work for others.<br /> <br /> Or better yet, why not a crossover setting focusing on WWII? How did it effect the supernaturals? How did THEY effect it? Just thought I'd throw that out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't mind that. After reading the myths and legends of WWII and how Nazi Germany was supposedly conducting occult research and experiments would be an interesting era for the supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T17:08:54-08:00","id":403873,"title":"","content":"I dunno Civil War era werewolf could be great. I'd love to see what the Uratha were like during the Peloponnesian Wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T17:32:45-08:00","id":403922,"title":"","content":"For Werewolf my top picks in chronological order...<br /> <br /> - Vedic era: an era where spirits still walk openly to be worshipped by mortals, the forsaken (treated as unclean outcasts by spirit and mortal worlds alike) fight back this tide of Asura<br /> - Forsaken by Rome: part of a multi-splat line of companion pieces to Requiem for Rome <br /> - Meiji Restoration: notably the era where the Japanese Wolf and the Samurai tradition both were eliminated<br /> - Boxer Rebellion: a crossover setting with Geist, focusing on Spirit &amp; Ancestor possession","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T17:35:57-08:00","id":403924,"title":"","content":"Greenlandic werewolves during the Little Ice Age. The Storm Lords are thriving, as are the Thule, the Norsemen are leaving the island for more hospitable climes, the land is freezing, the sea is vengeful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}